flowchart TB
  accTitle: When a comment folds a summary for the maintainers
  accDescr: The AI answers in the reporter's language and also writes a summary for the maintainers in the language of [maintainers] language, English by default. When the answer is in the maintainers' language, the apply job leaves the summary out and says so in the log; so does an empty summary, and the comment on a possible vulnerability never has one. Otherwise the comment ends with the summary, cleaned as every text of the AI, folded under a line from the maintainers' catalog, such as For the maintainers, in English, and its hidden marker records maint=en.
  ai["`**The AI** answers in the<br>reporter's language and writes<br>a summary for the maintainers`"] --> same{"the answer in the language<br>of [maintainers] language?"}
  same -- "yes" --> left["left out, with a<br>notice in the log"]
  same -- "no, such as Japanese" --> empty{"a summary, and no<br>possible vulnerability?"}
  empty -- "no" --> none["no fold"]
  empty -- "yes" --> clean["cleaned as every<br>text of the AI"]
  clean --> fold["`folded below the comment:<br>**For the maintainers, in English**`"]
  fold --> marker["the hidden marker<br>records maint=en"]
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  class same,empty question
  class ai,left,none,clean job
  class fold,marker safe
